WEBVTT

0
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.680
How are you, children?

1
00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.440
We are doing fine!

2
00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:55.600
You may sit.

3
00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.440
Thank you, teacher!

4
00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.120
Let's start on three!

5
00:01:09.480 --> 00:01:12.680
One, two, three.

6
00:01:51.440 --> 00:01:55.040
Lotus flowers...

7
00:01:58.000 --> 00:01:59.320
Silence!

8
00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:04.480
Lotus flowers...

9
00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:18.800
Lotus flowers...

10
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.600
Lotus flowers...

11
00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:37.520
...are blossoming...

12
00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:48.840
...I am happy.

13
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.840
You might think
there's no use of singing the Smot.

14
00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:25.680
That's not true!
We have to learn it together attentively.

15
00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.000
Smot is important to everyone.

16
00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:36.480
It changes our behavior,
educates our speech and soul,

17
00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.600
so that we would be polite.

18
00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:44.040
We have to respect one another!

19
00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:52.040
Therefore we have to learn carefully
and remember it together.

20
00:03:52.280 --> 00:03:56.760
Smot is an important song
that teaches us to respect the elderly,

21
00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:02.080
our parents and relatives.

22
00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:08.320
If we think about it carefully,

23
00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:13.080
we are going to understand
the real meaning of it.

24
00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.840
"Parents are our first teachers" -
have we learned that song already?

25
00:04:19.920 --> 00:04:21.920
Not yet!
- Not yet?

26
00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:26.960
"Parents are our first teachers"
is very educational.

27
00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.080
Would you like me to sing it for you?

28
00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:47.280
Parents are our very first teachers.

29
00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:59.040
They are the best teachers in the world.

30
00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:08.440
One might say that
they are the real Theravada.

31
00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:53.360
My name is Suon Srey Oun.
I am 35 years old.

32
00:05:54.960 --> 00:06:02.080
I am a farmer
and a dharma chant (Smot) teacher.

33
00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:17.960
When I was young, I used to listen  
people chanting at the funerals.

34
00:06:21.880 --> 00:06:26.880
Smot is very important to me.

35
00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.240
It makes me happy.

36
00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.480
It gives my life meaning.

37
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:38.480
Buddhist dharma is all I have.

38
00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:51.800
Dharma makes people
considerable  towards one another.

39
00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:58.400
Although we have Smot, people still  
don't know how to respect each other.

40
00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.200
This does not help
our country to develop.

41
00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.840
Again! One, two three...

42
00:13:29.720 --> 00:13:33.000
I am the oldest of my sisters.

43
00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:39.040
That's why I need to help
my parents to make a living.

44
00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:49.200
I have had a very rough life
since my childhood.

45
00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:53.400
I am not totally free.

46
00:13:58.680 --> 00:14:05.240
She carries water, collects the firewood,
cooks, cleans, feeds the cows.

47
00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:08.480
She does everything.

48
00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:14.080
She helps us with all the chores
at the times she is not teaching.

49
00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:30.160
When my children were small,

50
00:14:30.400 --> 00:14:39.080
we use to carry water
to the vegetables 50-70 times per day.

51
00:14:39.200 --> 00:14:46.160
Now we are old and ill
from all the overworking.

52
00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:57.440
We struggled a lot. My life got
better when my children grew up.

53
00:15:45.600 --> 00:15:55.040
We provide 9 long carpets, 20 big carpets
 and 40 carpets for the monks.

54
00:15:55.800 --> 00:16:05.200
Also materials, decorations,
drinks and 2 days of service.

55
00:16:06.600 --> 00:16:14.040
I don't make a profit from it.
 It is for gasoline only.

56
00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:05.320
My name is Pheun Srey Pov.

57
00:17:05.480 --> 00:17:10.200
People also know me as Srey Pov Smot,

58
00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:15.800
because I sing Smot
at different ceremonies.

59
00:17:23.960 --> 00:17:30.000
I think I was the first one
to create such a business.

60
00:17:30.760 --> 00:17:38.840
Old people always help each other
organize the ceremonies.

61
00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:47.080
They have never thought
about earning a living from it.

62
00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:56.800
For me, singing Smot
 doesn't have a price.

63
00:17:57.040 --> 00:18:06.120
If I had some kind of office job,

64
00:18:06.440 --> 00:18:11.160
I couldn't sing Smot.

65
00:18:16.200 --> 00:18:18.360
Your lips are so pale!

66
00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:23.520
So pale. So pale.

67
00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:47.040
I used to be just a regular girl,
a simple Smot singer.

68
00:18:47.200 --> 00:18:58.400
At school, I learned general knowledge
 and English, like other children.

69
00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:09.080
Now I have a permanent job
at the Buddhist sector.

70
00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:20.640
I am recognized by Buddhist people
and by people, I have worked for.

71
00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:28.000
There is a big difference since

72
00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:38.640
I was supported by my parents
and the organization.

73
00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:50.960
Now I make my own living and
offer jobs to younger generation.

74
00:20:21.240 --> 00:20:25.680
Mother feels relieved,

75
00:20:31.920 --> 00:20:37.200
even if she is unhappy and tired.

76
00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:43.160
Mother feels better.

77
00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:47.480
Now, both of you together.

78
00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.520
Teacher, please lead us!

79
00:20:54.640 --> 00:20:58.520
I feel for the mother.

80
00:21:16.600 --> 00:21:20.240
It sounds so sad,
 I cannot sing it now.

81
00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:24.480
Under the rain and thunder...

82
00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:30.760
No, you're confused -
please repeat!

83
00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:45.680
We went to visit
 our grandparents and relatives.

84
00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:55.600
My teacher makes me laugh,
 I cannot sing Smot now.

85
00:21:56.760 --> 00:22:02.040
I smile because I'm satisfied now.
You can sing Smot very well.

86
00:22:03.480 --> 00:22:07.960
My teacher knows my weakness.
I can't sing Smot when you laugh.

87
00:22:11.800 --> 00:22:14.560
I am just really happy!

88
00:22:15.720 --> 00:22:20.480
Students who want to become

89
00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:29.880
the masters or teachers,
 need to be focused and patient.

90
00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:34.880
If they are not committed,

91
00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:40.000
they won't be able to make it
because Smot is complicated.

92
00:22:50.120 --> 00:22:58.000
I know Smot since I was
because my father used to sing Smot.

93
00:22:58.160 --> 00:23:01.120
I started to learn from him.

94
00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:11.040
The history of Smot started when  
Buddha compiled a teaching for us.

95
00:23:12.920 --> 00:23:20.880
When I was 17, the Pol Pot regime
started and Smot was not allowed.

96
00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:28.280
They banned it completely,
we had to whisper Smot.

97
00:23:28.560 --> 00:23:36.160
I practiced Smot whispering
so that nobody would hear.

98
00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:42.720
If they had heard us singing Smot,  
they would have captured us.

99
00:23:44.000 --> 00:23:48.800
They didn't care whether
 it was a night or day.

100
00:23:49.640 --> 00:23:58.000
They would have caught
and killed us immediately.

101
00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:07.240
After Pol Pot, joyful times began.
There was no more sadness.

102
00:24:08.440 --> 00:24:13.840
We were freed from Pol Pot
and Buddhism returned.

103
00:24:16.280 --> 00:24:21.240
People and Buddha followers
were all happy.

104
00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:29.840
I was confident enough to
start singing Smot again.

105
00:24:31.520 --> 00:24:36.360
I was afraid that the Khmer
culture would fade away.

106
00:24:37.080 --> 00:24:42.240
I tried to teach the younger generation  
so they could teach the next generation.

107
00:24:42.560 --> 00:24:46.840
I wanted to make sure
that our culture wouldn't be lost -

108
00:24:46.920 --> 00:24:48.920
that's why I made an effort.

109
00:25:04.440 --> 00:25:10.920
I taught almost 10 years.

110
00:25:11.080 --> 00:25:17.360
8 out of 10 students were successful.

111
00:25:17.600 --> 00:25:25.680
If they had the skills like
Srey Oun and Srey Pov do.

112
00:25:31.960 --> 00:25:38.440
After I retired, I
assigned Srey Oun to teach.

113
00:25:38.880 --> 00:25:47.040
She now has a job
 because I taught her.

114
00:26:55.000 --> 00:27:01.120
Dharma is the blessing sound
of success.

115
00:27:01.920 --> 00:27:09.000
The golden discipline
has the highest value.

116
00:27:13.000 --> 00:27:19.520
Praying is like the golden silk.

117
00:27:20.560 --> 00:27:28.360
When I was learning to chant Smot,
I was offered a scholarship.

118
00:27:28.640 --> 00:27:33.560
I wanted to move to Phnom Penh
to become a traditional singer.

119
00:27:39.080 --> 00:27:49.320
I listened to beautiful songs by
Sin Sisamuth and Ros Sereysothea.

120
00:27:49.800 --> 00:27:53.640
I wished I could sing
just like them.

121
00:27:54.200 --> 00:27:58.000
I like to sing
but I don't dare dream too big

122
00:27:58.080 --> 00:28:02.760
because I don't have
the education for it.

123
00:28:08.680 --> 00:28:12.720
Our living conditions
and family  status weren't very good.

124
00:28:13.800 --> 00:28:17.240
There was nobody
to  help out our parents.

125
00:28:17.400 --> 00:28:20.440
After failing
the  9th grade final exam,

126
00:28:20.520 --> 00:28:23.360
I quit school to
 help my parents.

127
00:28:26.800 --> 00:28:33.360
Our children work in a factory and give
 away their salary to support the family.

128
00:28:33.800 --> 00:28:43.800
We live a much better life now compared
to the past when the children were young.

129
00:28:53.760 --> 00:29:05.600
If I had continued studying
I would   have a better life like others.

130
00:29:40.400 --> 00:29:44.320
Young girls in my village get
married at the age of 17 to 18.

131
00:29:44.640 --> 00:29:48.800
I will be 36 this year and
soon I will be 40 years old.

132
00:29:49.480 --> 00:29:56.200
If I do get married, then hopefully
to a normal man, because I'm not pretty.

133
00:29:56.920 --> 00:30:02.720
I want a man with a good personality,
I don't care about the looks.

134
00:30:04.960 --> 00:30:10.520
I would be satisfied with a good personality
because I'm not pretty either.

135
00:30:11.040 --> 00:30:13.760
I am so worried about
my daughter's future.

136
00:30:14.080 --> 00:30:17.200
If she doesn't get married,

137
00:30:17.400 --> 00:30:22.880
I hope that her nephew
is going to take care of her.

138
00:30:23.360 --> 00:30:27.920
I don't want my daughters
to go far away from me.

139
00:30:28.440 --> 00:30:34.400
I'm afraid that they'll have
problems with the in-laws.

140
00:30:34.640 --> 00:30:44.440
It is going to be good,
if her husband believes in her,

141
00:30:44.800 --> 00:30:52.400
but what if he listens to his mother?

142
00:30:52.680 --> 00:31:00.560
I have seen daughters living with
their in-laws and having problems.

143
00:31:03.400 --> 00:31:10.240
Sometimes they come back crying.

144
00:31:10.720 --> 00:31:15.280
I don't know what the future brings.

145
00:31:15.640 --> 00:31:17.760
If I am going to get married or not.

146
00:31:18.240 --> 00:31:22.640
If not, I need my nephew
to live with me.

147
00:31:25.440 --> 00:31:27.120
I believe in Karma.

148
00:31:27.720 --> 00:31:30.000
If I do a lot of good,

149
00:31:30.080 --> 00:31:34.200
my nephews will grow up fine.

150
00:31:35.000 --> 00:31:37.080
When I get old,

151
00:31:37.160 --> 00:31:41.160
they take care of me

152
00:31:41.240 --> 00:31:47.560
as their biological mother.

153
00:32:09.880 --> 00:32:19.640
In Cambodia, parents always
worry about their daughters.

154
00:32:19.960 --> 00:32:30.240
When the daughter grows up,
they always fix her up with a man.

155
00:32:33.880 --> 00:32:45.840
Normally they get married at the age
of 18 or 19 and have children.

156
00:32:46.240 --> 00:32:56.840
Some of my friends are married
and   their children go to school already.

157
00:32:57.280 --> 00:33:07.680
After graduating from college,
I wanted to be successful at my work.

158
00:33:08.600 --> 00:33:19.680
When I got 25, my parents started
talking to me about marriage.

159
00:33:20.080 --> 00:33:27.360
I asked for more time
to be independent.

160
00:33:27.680 --> 00:33:36.680
I want to stay single,
independent and happy.

161
00:33:36.960 --> 00:33:45.080
If I get married I would soon
be tied up with children.

162
00:33:45.360 --> 00:33:50.280
I don't want that at the moment.

163
00:33:50.480 --> 00:33:56.040
Luckily my parents understand me.

164
00:33:56.120 --> 00:34:01.920
I can stay single
 without any pressure.

165
00:34:28.920 --> 00:34:32.640
I would like to ask the
 whole family to gather here.

166
00:34:32.760 --> 00:34:38.720
We are starting with the "Asking for
parents' forgiveness" ceremony.

167
00:34:39.800 --> 00:34:45.000
Madams, have you already
prepared new clothes for her?

168
00:34:45.240 --> 00:34:49.960
These are already here?
 I am going to prepare these.

169
00:34:50.160 --> 00:34:53.480
Madam, you should also
prepare some money.

170
00:34:53.800 --> 00:34:57.000
You can relax now.
Are you ok?

171
00:35:01.880 --> 00:35:04.920
Please help her!

172
00:35:05.840 --> 00:35:08.960
Let her stand up slowly by herself.

173
00:35:16.840 --> 00:35:23.760
Before we start chanting
the Buddhist dharma song.

174
00:35:24.680 --> 00:35:28.880
I would like to pay respect
to the Three Jewels.

175
00:35:29.440 --> 00:35:34.000
Special respect to the ceremony owners

176
00:35:34.080 --> 00:35:37.640
and all the Buddhism followers.

177
00:35:38.720 --> 00:35:48.480
Please accept this dharma chanting as
a  respect of our our parents' good deeds.

178
00:35:53.080 --> 00:36:00.800
I bow down in respect and
raise my hands to ask for forgiveness.

179
00:36:01.960 --> 00:36:06.040
I am asking forgiveness for everything
 I have done wrong since I was young.

180
00:36:06.400 --> 00:36:10.080
My body and mind ache because of

181
00:36:11.440 --> 00:36:18.560
all my careless words,
ignorance and stubbornness.

182
00:36:19.320 --> 00:36:22.600
Because of all my inappropriate behavior.

183
00:36:23.240 --> 00:36:33.360
I feel enlightenment and
 I am starting to understand now.

184
00:36:34.200 --> 00:36:40.560
I am forever grateful to you.

185
00:36:45.080 --> 00:36:52.440
Mother, father, I feel dolors.

186
00:37:03.440 --> 00:37:20.200
Since I was born you have worried
about me and taken care of me.

187
00:37:39.560 --> 00:37:49.120
It is time to ask for forgiveness
from your mother.

188
00:37:49.320 --> 00:37:54.080
Speak out from your mind.

189
00:37:54.880 --> 00:37:58.680
Please express your respect,

190
00:37:58.760 --> 00:38:05.440
gratitude and love.

191
00:38:07.920 --> 00:38:18.120
The truth is hidden
 in the words of children.

192
00:38:20.400 --> 00:38:34.280
We would like to ask for forgiveness
on behalf of all the grandchildren.

193
00:38:34.640 --> 00:38:45.840
We wish that you live
 a healthy and long life.

194
00:38:48.200 --> 00:38:54.880
We love you so much!

195
00:40:21.000 --> 00:40:28.040
Respecting parents is something
that is always on my mind.

196
00:40:28.400 --> 00:40:35.440
I don't need a big ceremony
to express that.

197
00:40:35.800 --> 00:40:41.280
I always bring good news
 and results to my parents.

198
00:40:41.560 --> 00:40:48.320
Since I was young,
 whether in high school or in college,

199
00:40:48.560 --> 00:40:52.000
I have never failed an exam.

200
00:40:52.640 --> 00:40:56.000
I never disappoint them.

201
00:40:56.320 --> 00:41:00.640
This woman is mature.

202
00:41:01.320 --> 00:41:05.320
She loves traditions.

203
00:41:05.840 --> 00:41:11.240
How many young women are
interested in things like that?

204
00:41:11.800 --> 00:41:14.080
Only her!

205
00:41:14.360 --> 00:41:23.600
She can manage the monks, gifts,  
monks' places, everything.

206
00:41:55.920 --> 00:42:00.400
I now ask for your forgiveness.

207
00:42:06.120 --> 00:42:11.040
For all I have done
to you, my parents.

208
00:42:20.080 --> 00:42:24.640
For all my careless words.

209
00:42:28.080 --> 00:42:32.400
Parents, please forgive me!

210
00:42:48.840 --> 00:42:54.280
Mother and father do a lot of good.

211
00:43:01.040 --> 00:43:06.400
I offer my body and words.

212
00:43:12.400 --> 00:43:17.160
And bow down to express my respect.

213
00:43:22.000 --> 00:43:29.200
This song reminds me of the day
I celebrated a ceremony for my mother.

214
00:43:29.920 --> 00:43:32.400
I started to sing this song,
 but couldn't finish it,

215
00:43:32.480 --> 00:43:34.480
because I started crying.

216
00:43:44.120 --> 00:43:54.080
It reminds me of the mistakes
I have made concerning my parents.

217
00:43:55.360 --> 00:44:03.360
I celebrated the ceremony
and chanted this song...

218
00:44:03.640 --> 00:44:10.800
...I started crying
already during the first paragraph.

219
00:44:28.880 --> 00:44:32.800
I haven't had many
 happy moments in my life.

220
00:44:34.080 --> 00:44:37.600
I have been working very hard
since childhood.

221
00:44:38.040 --> 00:44:43.600
Living together with my whole family  
is my happiness.

222
00:44:44.960 --> 00:44:52.320
I am going to stay here forever
and take care of them with respect.

223
00:45:59.720 --> 00:46:07.280
Nowadays, everybody lives with the
purpose to keep their body alive.

224
00:46:07.880 --> 00:46:13.480
Death is unpredictable.
No one can escape from it.

225
00:46:14.600 --> 00:46:18.880
That's why we sing Smot to people
to make them think about it.

226
00:46:19.040 --> 00:46:21.920
After we die,
we are like a piece of firewood.

227
00:46:22.000 --> 00:46:25.640
Only our soul flies away from the body.

228
00:46:25.960 --> 00:46:29.440
Our body is like a house
where the soul stays.

229
00:46:29.760 --> 00:46:32.560
When the soul leaves,
the house burns down

230
00:46:32.640 --> 00:46:37.560
a nd the soul flies away
to find a new house.

231
00:46:38.480 --> 00:46:41.080
If you are a good person,
you go to heaven.

232
00:46:41.160 --> 00:46:45.240
If they are bad,
they go deep into the Earth.

233
00:46:45.920 --> 00:46:49.280
Inside the Earth,
they become evil demons.

234
00:46:49.840 --> 00:46:53.880
This is according to the Cambodian belief
 as well as the Buddhist belief.

235
00:47:06.040 --> 00:47:11.400
Eight big Jewel places.

236
00:47:25.760 --> 00:47:33.800
Praised by all kinds of animals.

237
00:47:48.120 --> 00:47:56.280
The first Jewel is the quiet Lumbini park.

238
00:48:08.320 --> 00:48:14.320
That's where Buddha was born.

239
00:48:29.200 --> 00:48:35.320
The second is the place
of enlightenment.

240
00:48:50.280 --> 00:48:59.800
Under the Jewel fig tree.

241
00:49:11.640 --> 00:49:19.560
The third is the place...

242
00:49:21.640 --> 00:49:28.240
...where Buddha taught Dharma...

